Faisal, Seth,

a)=A0 DFS:
Qatar specifies EN302 502 for their upper band and that spec states to appl=
y radar detection in 5725-5850 (but not 5850-5875).=A0=A0=A0 Rather than cr=
eate a more complicated definition, I propose we leave the patch as it curr=
ently is. Just means the last channel will also have radar detection enable=
d.=A0 =A0If you want to review that spec, just google "EN 302 502".=A0 You =
will find latest V2.0.8 or V2.1.1=A0 (both have same DFS rules).

(5725 - 5875 @ 80), (50 mW), NO-OUTDOOR, DFS


b) Power Limits:
I encourage the use of the higher power limits per the previously shared CR=
A Confirmation doc.=A0 They did not yet get around to updating their websit=
e with these latest rules. But in my opinion, this document is an unequivoc=
al confirmation of what the current rules are.=A0=A0=A0=A0 The attached doc=
 states the date, the authority, the specs and the limits.=A0=A0 The web si=
te has outdated information.

I propose the patch be released per attached CRA confirmation doc:

(2400 - 2483.5 @ 40), (100 mW), NO-OUTDOOR
(5150 - 5250 @ 80), (200 mW), NO-OUTDOOR, AUTO-BW
(5250 - 5350 @ 80), (200 mW), NO-OUTDOOR, DFS, AUTO-BW
(5470 - 5725 @ 160), (100 mW), NO-OUTDOOR, DFS
(5725 - 5875 @ 80), (100 mW), NO-OUTDOOR, DFS
(57000 - 66000 @ 2160), (40), NO-OUTDOOR

Please send comments if any, since customer is waiting for updated definiti=
on to propagate as soon as possible.


Thanks,

Michael Green


